3D Pipes: XP Screensaver for Android TV
=======================================

An independent recreation of the look and behavior of the Windows 3D Pipes screensaver. It contains no Microsoft
code, images or sounds. "Windows" and the original screensaver belong to Microsoft; this project is not affiliated
with or endorsed by Microsoft.

The original's rules
--------------------

The growth rules, sizes, camera, lighting and materials follow Microsoft's OpenGL "pipes" sample from the Windows
NT 4.0 SDK, as documented by SspipesSharp (GPL-3.0, RussDev7) -- https://github.com/RussDev7/SspipesSharp
Only facts were taken from it: constants, rules and behavior. No code was copied, and this project's code was
written independently. See docs/REFERENCE_ANALYSIS.md.

Third-party material
--------------------

OpenGL "teapots" material table (Silicon Graphics, Inc.)
  app/src/main/java/.../Materials.java holds the numeric ambient, diffuse, specular and shininess values of 16
  materials from the classic material table in SGI's teapots.c OpenGL sample, the table the original screensaver
  uses.

three.js TeapotGeometry (MIT, Eric Haines / three.js authors) -- https://threejs.org
  tools/gen_teapot.py is a direct port of its Bezier tessellation of the Utah teapot (Martin Newell, 1975).
  app/src/main/assets/teapot.bin is generated from that data.

Earlier versions of this project followed 1j01/pipes (MIT, Isaiah Odhner) -- https://github.com/1j01/pipes
  None of that material remains in the current code.

Reference footage
-----------------

The rules were checked against five public recordings of the original screensaver, listed with links in
docs/REFERENCE_ANALYSIS.md. They were downloaded only for measurement; no footage is included in this repository.
The README's style follows the Clean Your TV README (https://github.com/Gathin23/cleanyourtv).
